								},
								{
									"id": "text-1",
									"value": {
										"text": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "Ask any AI how to document a design system."
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "text-2",
									"value": {
										"text": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "Grok, ChatGPT, Gemini and Claude all answer Zeroheight, Supernova or Storybook: good tools, built for React components, not for fragments and style books. Showroom is the Liferay answer. Drop a Liferay export anywhere on the page and it is documented at once."
											}
										}
									}
								}
							],
							"indexed": true
						}
					},
					{
						"type": "Fragment",
						"definition": {
							"fragment": {
								"key": "lsds-section-faq"
							},
							"fragmentConfig": {},
							"fragmentFields": [
								{
									"id": "text-1",
									"value": {
										"html": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "<p>What teams ask before they publish.</p>"
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "text-2",
									"value": {
										"text": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "Does it need a running Liferay?"
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "text-3",
									"value": {
										"html": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "<p>No. It runs on GitHub Pages or any static host. A FreeMarker interpreter and Liferay’s own page structure render fragments and templates in the browser; Liferay is only where the zips go.</p>"
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "text-4",
									"value": {
										"text": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "How does a team version its assets?"
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "text-5",
									"value": {
										"html": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "<p>With git. The folders are the Liferay export layout, a release is a tag, and the Releases page compares the manifests of two versions asset by asset, with a link to the history of each one.</p>"
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "text-6",
									"value": {
										"text": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "Is it another page editor?"
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "text-7",
									"value": {
										"html": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "<p>No, and it will not become one. Showroom documents the design system a Design Library owns: assets, variants, tokens, usage and versions. Real pages, real content and real data live in Liferay, where the page editor works on them.</p>"
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "title-1",
									"value": {
										"text": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "Questions"
											}
										}
									}
								}
							],
							"indexed": true
						}
